        "original_id": "299c9ba8-f71f-518a-9682-903d3372525b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Anaïs Nin, Odysseas Elytis\n- Works: The Four-Chambered Heart, Cities of the Interior\n- Awards: Nobel Prize in Literature\n- Topics: romantic modernism\n\nFacts:\n- Anaïs Nin was born as Angela Anaïs Juana Antolina Rosa Edelmira Nin y Culmell on February 21, 1903.\n- Anaïs Nin was born in France to Cuban parents and was also raised in France.\n- Odysseas Elytis, the pen name of Odysseas Alepoudellis, was born on November 2, 1911.\n- Odysseas Elytis was regarded as a major exponent of romantic modernism in Greece and internationally.\n- The Four-Chambered Heart is a 1950 autobiographical novel by French-born writer Anaïs Nin.\n- The Four-Chambered Heart is part of Anaïs Nin's Cities of the Interior sequence.\n- Odysseas Elytis received the Nobel Prize in Literature in 1979.\n- Anaïs Nin died on January 14, 1977.\n- Odysseas Elytis died on March 18, 1996.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
